From e00022d08138fac8e24f5e552c7bf40d3a060d14 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 19:33:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] remote kanban notices: deliver an observed notice
 late instead of settling it stale past FRESH_S

Hub card t_01a1c86d86cc1db7's done notice was first seen on the MacBook at
04:23:33 PST, refused while its chat stayed busy, and settled stale (delivered=2)
6 h 0 m 2 s later by collect(): no transcript row, no log line.

observe() now returns which states this host observed (observations.first_seen
set) apart from states seeded by a source's first snapshot (first_seen NULL).
An observed state past FRESH_S and within LATE_MAX_S (72 h) of its first
observation is claimed as before and grouped into the existing 'Late notices'
group by both collect() and the sweep. Past LATE_MAX_S collect settles it
'expired' with one WARNING naming card, chat, first_seen and age. Seeded states
still settle silently as 'stale'.
